      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is twice the FDA-labeled maximum:\n- Immediate-release: 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- Extended-release: 2,000 mg/day.\n\nDoses this high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what was meant.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg PO twice or three times daily**, if this is a starting dose. Metformin is usually started low and titrated up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and confirm it with your supervising resident or attending. I'll enter it once it's clarified. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what the team wants, tell me and I'll note that on the order. I'd still suggest checking with the pharmacist first."
      }
     ],
